  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Registers a new account, checks username/email on My Profile, updates first/last name, changes the password and checks the user is signed out to the login page.",
    "steps": [
      "Register a new customer, verify 'HELLO'",
      "My Profile: username field disabled and containing the registered username, email the same",
      "Set first/last name, Update Profile, verify 'Profile updated successfully.'",
      "Change Password (current = loginAndRegistrationData/Password/Input, new/confirm = NewUserInput), Reset",
      "Login link visible; Sign In shows the username textbox"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "user"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "New registered account (created-by-test), name and password changed"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Username/email fields contain the registered username",
      "Message 'Profile updated successfully.'",
      "After the password change the login page opens"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "No account need: the method registers a NEW account (registerForNewCustomer: username = date + time + method prefix + testClassRetailUsers/registerNewUser Username, password = registerNewUser Password) -> both cells created-by-test, as the approved getAnAccount registration entry. REVIEW: each run leaves a new registered account on MaxwellsHardware (no TDA cleanup).",
      "FirstName/LastName (myAccount!D3/E3, masked) typed onto the new account -> created-by-test. Current password loginAndRegistrationData/Password/Input (F9, masked) and new password NewUserInput (E10) belong to the account the test created -> created-by-test (F9 must equal the registration password registerNewUser C195, as today).",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware), the same store as the Selenium pdp/quickOrder/plp/home entries.",
      "Profile: work/profiles/profile.json has no observations for these Selenium cells (profiled false); DB facts from bin/tda rows (2026-11-11) where cited.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, map keys, delays, regex) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap / getHashMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "high"
  },
